# rui — Capability Gate Verification

Verify the rui library builds and passes all tests across every gate.

## Worklist

Decomposed into mechanical sub-items, each under 10 minutes per haiku agent:

- [ ] [scout] [ask: gate-1] [cap: cap-build] Build debug: Run `cargo build -p rui`. Success = zero compilation errors, 0.20s elapsed
- [ ] [scout] [ask: gate-2] [cap: cap-fmt] Format check: Run `cargo fmt --check`. Success = zero formatting violations reported
- [ ] [scout] [ask: gate-3] [cap: cap-clippy] Lint check: Run `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`. Success = zero warnings reported
- [ ] [scout] [ask: gate-4] [cap: cap-tests] Library tests: Run `cargo test -p rui --lib`. Success = 260+ tests pass, 0 failures
- [ ] [scout] [ask: gate-5] [cap: cap-examples] Example counter: Run `cargo run -p rui --example counter --release` and exit. Success = runs without panic or error code ≠ 0

## Rationale

Original item tried to verify all gates at once, exceeding 20-minute wall time budget. Each sub-item is independent (no dependencies between gates) and mechanical (verifiable by command output alone). Parallel execution by 5 haiku agents = 10 minutes wall time for the full gate suite.

Remaining gates (cap-wasm, cap-recipes, cap-a11y, cap-docs) are deferred to follow-up item once these 5 land.
